  "output": "Now I have enough information for a comprehensive analysis. Let me write the report.\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis: VoidRift\n\nHere are the concrete issues found, grouped by category, with file locations and fixes.\n\n---\n\n### 1. N+1 I/O Pattern: `IndexCache.save()` on every write\n\n**File:** `src/codemap/cache.ts:58`\n\nEvery call to `cache.set()` synchronously serializes and writes the entire JSON file. During indexing runs (e.g. on startup or after a file change triggers re-summarization), this fires once per file.\n\n```typescript\n// Current — N disk writes for N files indexed\npublic set(filePath: string, sha256: string, summary: string, totalLines: number): void {\n  this.data[filePath] = { sha256, summary, totalLines, lastIndexed: Date.now() };\n  this.save(); // entire file written here\n}\n```\n\n**Fix:** Add a dirty flag, expose a `flush()` method, and let the caller batch:\n\n```typescript\nprivate dirty = false;\n\npublic set(filePath: string, sha256: string, summary: string, totalLines: number): void {\n  this.data[filePath] = { sha256, summary, totalLines, lastIndexed: Date.now() };\n  this.dirty = true;\n}\n\npublic flush(): void {\n  if (!this.dirty) return;\n  const dir = join(this.cachePath, \"..\");\n  if (!existsSync(dir)) mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\n  writeFileSync(this.cachePath, JSON.stringify(this.data, null, 2));\n  this.dirty = false;\n}\n```\n\nThen in `graph.ts` after the indexing loop, call `cacheInstance.flush()` once. For the debounced re-index case in `cli.ts`, use `cache.flush()` after `setCodeMap`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Redundant Filesystem Walk: `generateCodeMap` vs `getCodeMapEntries`\n\n**File:** `src/codemap/index.ts:24-31`, `src/bootstrap/cli.ts:67,182`\n\nBoth exported functions call `walk()` independently. In `cli.ts`, `generateCodeMap` is called at startup (line 67) and again inside the debounced watcher callback (line 182). If any code path also calls `getCodeMapEntries`, the workspace is walked twice.\n\n```typescript\n// Both call walk() independently — no sharing\nexport function generateCodeMap(workspaceRoot: string): string {\n  return formatTree(walk(workspaceRoot, workspaceRoot, 0)); // walk #1\n}\nexport function getCodeMapEntries(workspaceRoot: string): CodeMapEntry[] {\n  return walk(workspaceRoot, workspaceRoot, 0); // walk #2\n}\n```\n\n**Fix:** Make `generateCodeMap` delegate through `getCodeMapEntries`:\n\n```typescript\nexport function getCodeMapEntries(workspaceRoot: string): CodeMapEntry[] {\n  return walk(workspaceRoot, workspaceRoot, 0);\n}\n\nexport function generateCodeMap(workspaceRoot: string): string {\n  return formatTree(getCodeMapEntries(workspaceRoot));\n}\n```\n\nIf both are needed in the same call site, compute entries once and format separately.\n\n---\n\n### 3. New Model Client Per Turn\n\n**File:** `src/turn.ts:44-45`, `src/adapters/factory.ts:77-85`\n\n`createTierAdapter` and `createAdapter` construct a `new ChatOpenAI / ChatAnthropic / ChatGoogleGenerativeAI` on every call. These constructors set up retry/timeout configuration and are invoked on every user turn, every fallback construction (`graph.ts:132`), every MCP sampling call (`cli.ts:77`), and every compact/summarize invocation.\n\n```typescript\n// turn.ts — new client on every turn\nconst resolved = isTierKey\n  ? createTierAdapter(tier as Tier, engine.container.config)\n  : createAdapter(tier, engine.container.config);\n```\n\n**Fix:** Memoize by `(modelName, configHash)`. Since config is static at runtime, keying by model name is sufficient:\n\n```typescript\n// factory.ts\nconst _clientCache = new Map<string, ResolvedModel>();\n\nexport function createAdapter(modelName: string, appConfig: VoidRiftConfig): ResolvedModel {\n  if (_clientCache.has(modelName)) return _clientCache.get(modelName)!;\n  const config = appConfig.models[modelName];\n  if (!config) throw new Error(`Model \"${modelName}\" not found in config`);\n  const resolved = { name: modelName, config, client: createClient(config, appConfig.maxConcurrentAgents) };\n  _clientCache.set(modelName, resolved);\n  return resolved;\n}\n```\n\nThe one edge case: `bindTools` in `graph.ts` wraps the client before use. The memoized value is the base client; `bindTools` produces a derived binding that should not be cached (it's tool-call-specific).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Memory Leak Risk: `STREAM_CHUNK_RECEIVED` subscription at debug level\n\n**File:** `src/logging/audit.ts:54-56`\n\nThe audit logger subscribes to `STREAM_CHUNK_RECEIVED` at `debug` level. This event fires for every token streamed — potentially hundreds of times per turn. The listener appends a log entry to disk synchronously on each event.\n\n```typescript\nunsubs.push(bus.subscribe(\"STREAM_CHUNK_RECEIVED\", (e) => {\n  this.local(\"debug\", \"model\", \"chunk\", e.payload); // disk write per token\n}));\n```\n\nThis is not a memory leak per se, but it's a per-token synchronous `appendFileSync` that degrades streaming throughput. At 50 tokens/s this is 50 synchronous disk writes/s. **Fix:** Only log at debug if debug mode is explicitly enabled, and buffer/batch writes:\n\n```typescript\n// Guard behind a flag\nif (this.opts.debugLevel === \"verbose\") {\n  unsubs.push(bus.subscribe(\"STREAM_CHUNK_RECEIVED\", (e) => {\n    this.local(\"debug\", \"model\", \"chunk\", e.payload);\n  }));\n}\n```\n\nSeparately, `attach()` returns an unsubscribe function but the caller (`cli.ts:173`) discards it — the 17 subscriptions are never torn down on `SESSION_END`. This is fine for a single-session CLI, but would leak in test environments that call `createEngine()` repeatedly.\n\n---\n\n### 5. `require(\"fs\")` Inside a Loop\n\n**File:** `src/bootstrap/validate.ts:41`\n\nDynamic `require()` inside a hot loop is unnecessary — the module is cached by Node after the first call, but the lookup overhead and code-smell of a CommonJS require in an ESM file is avoidable.\n\n```typescript\n// Current — require() called N times\nfor (const skill of skills.indexed) {\n  try {\n    const raw = require(\"fs\").readFileSync(skill.filePath, \"utf-8\"); // ← here\n```\n\n**Fix:** Import `readFileSync` at the top of the file:\n\n```typescript\nimport { readFileSync } from \"fs\"; // already used in sibling files via static import\n\n// ...in the loop:\nconst raw = readFileSync(skill.filePath, \"utf-8\");\n```\n\nSame pattern applies in `src/mcp/credentials.ts:62` (`require(\"fs\").unlinkSync`) and `src/session/brain.ts:127`.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Caching Opportunity: `summarizeFileWithFlash` Re-creates Adapter\n\n**File:** `src/codemap/summarizer.ts:33`\n\nEvery call to `summarizeFileWithFlash` calls `createTierAdapter(\"flash\", config)` and then assigns `resolved.client.cache = getModelCache()`. Since #3's fix memoizes the adapter, this becomes a no-op re-assignment of the same cache reference per call — but the `client.cache =` mutation on a cached instance is still a side-effect on a shared object. Move the cache assignment into `createClient()` or `createAdapter()` once:\n\n```typescript\n// factory.ts — set cache at construction time\nimport { getModelCache } from \"./cache.js\";\n\nfunction createClient(config: ModelConfig, maxConcurrency?: number): BaseChatModel {\n  const client = /* ... existing switch ... */;\n  (client as any).cache = getModelCache(); // assign once at construction\n  return client;\n}\n```\n\nThen remove the `resolved.client.cache = getModelCache()` line from `summarizer.ts`.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Table\n\n| Issue | File | Impact | Fix complexity |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `IndexCache.save()` per write | `codemap/cache.ts:58` | N disk writes during indexing | Low — dirty flag + `flush()` |\n| Double `walk()` | `codemap/index.ts:24-31` | 2× FS traversal | Trivial — delegate through `getCodeMapEntries` |\n| New model client per turn | `adapters/factory.ts:77` | Allocations + constructor overhead per turn | Low — Map cache keyed by model name |\n| Per-token `appendFileSync` at debug | `logging/audit.ts:54` | I/O bottleneck during streaming | Low — guard behind debug flag |\n| `require(\"fs\")` in loop | `bootstrap/validate.ts:41` | Minor — module lookup in hot path | Trivial — static import |\n| Cache assignment on shared instance | `codemap/summarizer.ts:33` | Minor mutation side-effect | Low — move into constructor |\n\nThe highest-ROI fixes are (1) and (3) — the cache write batching and model client memoization will be felt on every turn and every indexing pass.\n",
